    "message": "fix(clients): every plan sentence names the System model while the server drafts\n\nThe first delivery changed the line beside Draft plan and left the rest of the\nplan page saying the space's provider drafts it — the plan's empty body and\nthe Redraft… dialog named `local-vllm` while the card above them named the\nSystem model. The review of that delivery asked for the drafter to be fixed\nwherever the plan's copy names one, for the empty page's note to keep the half\nthat still holds, and for the native compile to be proved on CI.\n\n- `WIKI_PLAN_DRAFTER_SERVER` / `WikiPlanCopy.drafterServer` (\"System model\"):\n  taken by the empty page's body (`wikiPlanEmptyText`, `emptyText`), the\n  Redraft… dialog (`wikiPlanRedraftNote`, `redraftNote`) and the drafting\n  job's card (`wikiPlanJobCard`, `WikiPlanLogic.jobCard`) — the two ends read\n  one name from `src/shared/src/wiki-server-execution.fixture.json`;\n- the plan empty page's note keeps the sentence that still holds there:\n  `Runs on the server with the System model — usually 1–2 hours. Until you\n  confirm a plan, the Wiki shows its topic articles.`\n  (`WIKI_PLAN_EMPTY_NOTE_SERVER`, `WikiPlanCopy.emptyNoteServer`). Activity's\n  Plan card keeps the owner's short line, `System model · about 1–2 hours`;\n- the documents' build is P7's and is untouched;\n- tests: the web's lib and plan-page tests cover both modes for every sentence\n  (the empty page's body and note, the dialog, the drafting card), and\n  `WikiServerExecutionCopyParityTests` holds the native end to the web source\n  and the fixture; the plan/wiring parity tests moved with the signatures;\n- evidence: `docs/evidence/wiki-plan-server-note/` gains the plan empty page\n  under both modes, and `ci/` carries the client.yml probe that compiles the\n  three OrbitApp files the merge check cannot (`WikiPlanView.swift`,\n  `WikiDocScreens.swift`, `WikiModel.swift`).\n\nVerified: OrbitKit 3435 tests / 0 failures in docker swift:6.1, web vitest\n4743/4743, apiserver 4919/0, shared 406/406, compose topology 11/11.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
    "timestamp": "2026-10-08T10:06:14Z",
